Statement of modifications (GPL-3.0 section 5a)
-----------------------------------------------

Changes made to the original work:

1. Renamed throughout from "Mole" to "Nora", including the command name
   (`mo` -> `nr`, `mole` -> `nora`), environment variable prefixes, install
   paths, and all user-visible strings.

2. Added a macOS menubar application (`app/`). This is new work, not present
   upstream. It is a front end only: it executes the CLI as a subprocess and
   contains no cleanup or deletion logic of its own.

3. Performance changes to the CLI and its Go helpers:

   - lib/core/timeout.sh — the Perl timeout fallback polled with a fixed
     0.1s sleep, rounding every wrapped command up to at least 100ms. macOS
     ships no timeout(1), so all 127 call sites take this path. Replaced with
     an exponential backoff starting at 2ms.

   - nora (entrypoint) — subcommands that are only ever exec'd into now
     dispatch before the shared libraries are sourced. The target re-sources
     the same set in its own process, so the first load was discarded.

   - lib/clean/launch_services.sh — stale registrations were unregistered one
     `lsregister` call at a time. Now batched, with a per-path retry so the
     success and failure counts stay exact.

   - cmd/status/ — four caches (Bluetooth, power, trash size, GPU usage) had
     TTLs at or below the interval of their only caller, so none ever
     returned a cached value. Raised to match how fast the underlying data
     actually changes. powermetrics is no longer invoked when not running as
     root, where it can only fail.

   - cmd/analyze/scanner.go — folded directories (node_modules, .git, Caches,
     DerivedData and similar) bypassed the cache layer entirely and were
     re-measured with `du` on every scan. They now use the same cache, with
     the same freshness rules, as every other subtree.

4. Bug fix in cmd/status/metrics_battery.go — the `pmset` call passed
   context.Background(), making it the only unbounded subprocess in the
   collector; a wedged pmset would stall an entire snapshot. Now bounded.

5. Removed files specific to the upstream project and not applicable to a
   personal fork: release workflows and runbooks, contribution and security
   policy documents, contributor assets, agent configuration directories,
   and the tests covering that removed infrastructure.
